# CQ 14: Which service does an entity provide, and at which layer?
#
# Clause 5.2.2 has an entity of one layer provide a service to the layer above.
# That is the vertical relation of the architecture, and it is what makes a
# stack a stack rather than seven unrelated things.
#
# The layer is reported alongside, since a service means something only in
# relation to where it sits: the same name at layer 3 and at layer 7 describes
# different work.
#
# Only test case 2 answers. The others describe a communication without opening
# up its architecture, which the standard permits and question 08 reports.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?entity ?service ?layerNumber ?subsystem
WHERE {
  ?entity iso7498:providesService ?service .
  OPTIONAL { ?subsystem iso7498:hasEntity ?entity ;
                        iso7498:atLayer/iso7498:layerNumber ?layerNumber }
} ORDER BY DESC(?layerNumber) ?entity
